@FEAT-003
Feature: Cart management # test/validation_tests/features/cart_management.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to add, remove, and adjust items in my cart
  So that I can manage my order before checkout
  @TC-009 @US-005 @positive @high
  Scenario: Add an available item to the cart              # test/validation_tests/features/cart_management.feature:8
    Given the meal "Salmon Roll" is available              # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:76
    When the customer taps "Add to cart" on "Salmon Roll"  # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:88
    Then "Salmon Roll" appears in the cart with quantity 1 # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:93
    And the cart total is updated to include it            # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:98

  @TC-010 @US-005 @negative @high
  Scenario: Attempt to add an unavailable item                       # test/validation_tests/features/cart_management.feature:15
    Given the meal "Salmon Roll" is marked unavailable               # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:82
    When the customer attempts to add "Salmon Roll" to the cart      # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:106
    Then the item is not added to the cart                           # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:111
    And the customer sees a message that it is currently unavailable # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:116

  @TC-011 @US-007 @positive @medium
  Scenario: Increase and decrease item quantity                        # test/validation_tests/features/cart_management.feature:22
    Given "Salmon Roll" is already in the cart with quantity 1         # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:121
    When the customer increases the quantity by 2                      # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:129
    And the customer decreases the quantity by 1                       # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:135
    Then the cart shows "Salmon Roll" with quantity 2                  # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:141
    And the cart total is recalculated automatically after each change # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:146

  @TC-012 @US-006 @edge @medium
  Scenario: Decrease quantity to zero removes the item               # test/validation_tests/features/cart_management.feature:30
    Given "Salmon Roll" is the only item in the cart with quantity 1 # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:154
    When the customer decreases the quantity to 0                    # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:162
    Then "Salmon Roll" is removed from the cart entirely             # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:168
    And the cart total updates to zero                               # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:173
    And an empty-cart message is shown                               # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:178

  @TC-013 @US-005 @positive @high
  Scenario: Cart persists after a page reload                               # test/validation_tests/features/cart_management.feature:38
    Given the customer has added an item to the cart in the current session # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:184
    When the customer reloads the page                                      # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:192
    Then the cart still shows the same items and quantities                 # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:198

  @TC-014 @negative @high
  Scenario: Mix items from two different restaurants                           # test/validation_tests/features/cart_management.feature:44
    Given the cart contains an item from "Sushi Place"                         # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:203
    When the customer attempts to add an item from "Pizza Corner"              # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:211
    Then the app blocks the action                                             # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:218
    And the customer is prompted to start a new cart, clearing the current one # test/validation_tests/features/steps/cart_management_steps.py:223

